               .direct("Did you give {D.him} a chance to leave?", "\"Twenty minutes to pack. {D.He} refused.\""),
               .direct("What was your call about?", "\"The manager said {DL} had not paid for the week and had been told to leave by noon. {DL} refused, and the manager called us when it was past one.\""),
               .direct("What did the registration card say?", "\"'Transient guest. Weekly rate. Room must be vacated at checkout if unpaid.' {DL} signed it five weeks earlier.\""),
               .direct("What did {DL} say to you?", "\"That {D.he} had lived there more than a month and could only be evicted through the court. {D.He} asked for a court date and refused to pack.\""),
               .direct("What did you do before the arrest?", "\"I explained the manager's request, gave {DL} twenty minutes to pack, and told {D.him} what would happen if {D.he} did not. {D.He} said no.\""),
               .cross("{DL}'s son was enrolled in school using that room as his address.", "\"{D.He} showed me that when {D.he} came in, and the school paperwork matched.\""),
               .cross("{DL} had been there five weeks.", "\"That's what the receipts say.\""),
               .cross("{DL} had receipts for five weeks, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. Five weekly receipts for the same room, and a school enrollment form for {D.his} son that listed the motel as his home address.\""),
               .cross("The motel had a reason to clear that room, didn't it?", "\"I have heard that the motel wanted rooms for a construction crew paying more. I cannot say that was behind this one.\""),
               .cross("{DL} had been offered a shelter bed?", "\"So I learned later. {D.He} had been offered a free bed for the two of them that morning and turned it down.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} signed in as a transient guest, didn't pay, and refused to leave when told.",
                 "After five weeks, with a child enrolled in school from that room, it was {D.his} home. A tenant has the right to a court process."),
        allocution: "\"I had nowhere to go with my son, and I'd get paid in three days. I stayed past noon because I thought I could only be evicted by a court after a month. I should have asked for a few more days properly. I'm sorry to the manager and the deputies, and I'll pay what I owe.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been offered a free shelter bed for the two of them that morning and turned it down.",
                 "The motel had threatened to call deputies on two other long-stay families the same week to clear rooms for a construction crew paying more."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why didn't you leave?", "\"I had nowhere to go with my son. I got paid in three days.\""),
               .direct("Did you think you had a right to stay?", "\"After what happened at my apartment, I looked it up. I thought I did.\""),
               .direct("How long had you lived at the motel?", "\"About five weeks. After my earlier case I lost my apartment, and the motel was the only place I could afford for me and my son.\""),
               .direct("Why did you refuse to leave?", "\"I had nowhere to go with my son. My pay was due in three days, and the manager wanted me out at once.\""),
               .direct("What did you understand about your rights?", "\"After what happened with my apartment, I looked it up. I thought that after five weeks I was a tenant who could only be removed by a court.\""),
               .direct("Why did you turn down the shelter bed?", "\"It was one bed, and my son and I would have been split up. I did not want to leave him with strangers.\""),
               .cross("You signed a card saying you were a transient guest.", "\"I signed what they put in front of me.\""),
               .cross("You were told twice to leave.", "\"Yes. I was told twice to leave, and I didn't go the first time.\""),
               .cross("A court date would have taken weeks.", "\"I knew that. I just wanted to stay until payday, and I was going to pay the week.\""),
               .cross("You had been offered a free shelter bed that morning.", "\"I had, and I turned it down. It meant leaving my son with strangers for the night.\""),
                    .cross("You told the deputies you wanted a court date.", "\"I did. I thought a court had to order it, and I did not understand that the card changed that.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} and {D.his} son lived five weeks at a weekly motel, and when the week went unpaid the manager told {D} twice to leave by noon. {D} refused, deputies gave twenty minutes to pack, and {D} was arrested at 2 p.m.", "The defense will say that after five weeks, with a child enrolled in school from that room, the motel was {D}'s home. A tenant can only be removed through the court, and {D} was getting paid in three days."),
        closings: ("{D} signed a card calling {D.himself} a transient guest, was told twice to leave, and was given twenty minutes to pack. After {PRIOR}, {D} knew how a refusal to leave looks to a deputy.", "{D} had nowhere to go with a child, five weekly receipts, and a school form with the motel's address. The State must prove {D} was a guest and not a tenant who was owed a court date."),
