               .direct("Did you find a gun on {DL}?", "\"A loaded pistol in a holster on {D.his} hip.\""),
               .direct("What were you called to?", "\"A report that a man had pointed a gun at a driver in a grocery store lot. Several people were standing near a double-parked car when I arrived.\""),
               .direct("What did {V} tell you?", "\"That {V.he} double-parked behind {DL}'s truck to run in for a prescription. When {V.he} came back, {DL} was waiting, yelled, and drew a pistol through the windshield.\""),
               .direct("What did the cart attendant say?", "\"That {DL} 'pulled a gun and held it on the driver.' The attendant gave that statement at the scene, and signed it.\""),
               .direct("What was recovered?", "\"A loaded pistol in a holster on {DL}'s hip. A tire iron was also on the floor of the back seat of {V}'s car.\""),
               .cross("A tire iron was in {V}'s car.", "\"On the back seat floor. {V} says it's always there.\""),
               .cross("You can't see {V}'s hands on the video.", "\"Not behind the door. The door blocks the view, so I can't see {V.his} hands.\""),
               .cross("The video doesn't show the gun clearly, does it?", "\"It shows {DL}'s arm coming up level, with something in the hand. The cart attendant says it was a pistol, and the pistol was on {DL}'s hip.\""),
               .cross("Another camera caught more of what happened, didn't it?", "\"A phone video from the cart attendant turned up later. I have not been asked to say what it shows today.\""),
                    .cross("The cart attendant could not hear what was said?", "\"He was across the lot. He saw the arm come up and says it was a pistol, but he did not hear the words.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} pointed a pistol at a driver over a double-parked car.",
                 "{V} came at {D} with a tire iron; {D} only showed the gun to stop {V.him}."),
        allocution: "\"I told {V} to move, and {V.he} got out with a tire iron, and I put my hand on my gun. I never meant to point it at anyone. I was afraid, and I'm sorry that {V} was frightened. I wish we'd both just waited a minute.\"",
        truths: ("The cart attendant's phone video, found later, showed {V}'s hands empty when the pistol came up.",
                 "The cart attendant's phone video, found later, showed {V} coming around the door with the tire iron before {DL} reached for the gun."),
        defendant: [.direct("What happened?", "\"I told {V.him} to move. {V.He} got out with a tire iron. I put my hand on my gun and told {V.him} to stop.\""),
               .direct("Did you point it?", "\"I pulled it partway. I didn't point it.\""),
               .direct("Why were you waiting by your truck?", "\"{V} had double-parked behind me and blocked me in. I was in a hurry, and I had been standing there for several minutes.\""),
               .direct("What did you do?", "\"I put my hand on my gun and told {V.him} to stop. I pulled it partway out of the holster. I never pointed it at {V.him}.\""),
               .direct("Why did you touch your gun?", "\"I was afraid. A man with a tire iron was coming at me, and I thought it was the only way to stop him before he got to me.\""),
               .direct("Why did you carry a pistol?", "\"I have a permit, and I carry it every day. I had it on my hip at the grocery store like always.\""),
                    .cross("The video shows your arm level with {V}.", "\"That's my arm. It doesn't show what's in it.\""),
               .cross("The tire iron was on the floor of the back seat.", "\"{V.He} threw it back in when I drew.\""),
               .cross("You had a grudge about being blocked in.", "\"I was angry, and I will say so. I did not take out a gun because I was angry. I took out a gun because he had a tire iron.\""),
               .cross("You touched your gun before you knew what {V} had.", "\"I saw the tire iron as {V.he} came out of the car. I put my hand on the gun because I was afraid, not to threaten.\""),
               .cross("The cart attendant says you held the gun on {V}.", "\"He saw it from across the lot. I never pointed it, and I will say so under oath.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} double-parked behind {D}'s truck at a grocery store to run in for a prescription, and when {V.he} came back {D} was waiting. {V} says {D} yelled, then pointed a pistol through the windshield, and a cart attendant says {D} held it on the driver.", "The defense will say {V} came at {D} with a tire iron and {D} only put a hand on the holstered gun to stop {V.him}. The door blocks the camera, and the attendant's phone video shows how it began."),
        closings: ("The store camera shows {D}'s arm come up level toward {V}, a cart attendant saw a gun held on the driver, and a loaded pistol was on {D}'s hip. The earlier case, over {PRIOR}, had already shown {D} where this leads.", "{V} had a tire iron in the back seat and came around the car door at {D}. A man who touches his holster to stop an attacker is defending himself, and the State must prove {D} pointed it at {V}."),
        timeline: [(0, "{V} double-parks behind {DL}'s truck."), (0, "{V} returns; confrontation; pistol drawn."), (0, "Deputy arrives; pistol taken from {DL}.")],
        identified: "{V} wrote down {DL}'s plate; {DL} was still there when deputies arrived.",
        impact: "\"I was picking up my mother's heart medicine. I've never been so scared. I couldn't drive for an hour.\"",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "selfDefense"])

